# IMP Model Policy

1. Start with **Composer**. Remain on Composer while it is solving the task reliably.
2. Escalate to **Grok 4.6 High** only for demonstrated reasoning complexity,
   architectural reconciliation, difficult debugging, high-risk evidence-sensitive
   decisions, multi-agent synthesis, or material Composer failure/stall.
3. Do not escalate merely because a task is large, many files exist, Grok is
   available, or a prior task needed Grok. Prefer decomposition + Composer.
4. **Never use Fast model variants** (Composer Fast, Grok Fast, or any
   speed-optimized substitution that reduces reasoning quality). Use the
   normal/high-quality variant or do not use that family.
5. Parallel workers follow this ladder **individually**. One lane's escalation
   does not escalate the others.
6. Do not automatically assign Grok as orchestrator. Composer may orchestrate
   ordinary multi-agent work; escalate orchestration only when findings conflict
   or evidence-sensitive architecture must be decided.
7. Prefer the least expensive model that can perform the task correctly.
   Correctness and evidence integrity override model-cost optimization.

